+On a piecewise homogeneous domain with phasors defined under $\eim$, the vacuum-form Maxwell system is Eq.~\eqref{eq:ch1.maxwell-local}: Faraday's law $\curl\E=-\jj\omega\mu_0\H$ states that a time-varying magnetic flux drives a circulating electric field; Amp\`ere's law $\curl\H=\Jimp+\jj\omega\varepsilon_0\E$ states that impressed current and displacement current sustain magnetic circulation; Gauss's laws tie $\E$ and $\H$ to $\rho$ and enforce magnetic flux solenoidality \cite{maxwell1873,stratton1941}. Every subsequent operator is a compact restatement of these local relations together with boundary data on $\Gamma$ and, for open problems, outgoing selection at infinity.
